  "worked_solution": "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $Q$ is $p=\u27e8-1,0,4\u27e9$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=\u27e82,-4,1\u27e9$  and ${v}_{2}=\u27e80,-1,\\sqrt{3}\u27e9.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=\u27e8-1,0,4\u27e9+s\u27e82,-4,1\u27e9+t\u27e80,-1,\\sqrt{3}\u27e9,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
